0,Indigenous music of Australia - Wikipedia,https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Indigenous_music_of_Australia,"Indigenous music of Australia comprises the music of the Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander peoples of Australia, intersecting with their cultural and ceremonial observances, through the millennia of their individual and collective histories to the present day. [1][2][3][4] The traditional forms include many aspects of performance and ...",Wik Ngathan,Australian
1,Isaac Nathan - Wikipedia,https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Isaac_Nathan,"Isaac Nathan (1792 - 15 January 1864) [2] was an Anglo-Jewish emigre Australian musician, composer, musicologist, and music educator, who has been called the ""father of Australian music"", [3] having assisted the careers of numerous colonial musicians during his twenty-year residence in Australia. [4] He is best known for the success of his Hebrew Melodies (1815-1840) in London. [5] He ...",Wik Ngathan,Australian
2,Wik Ngathan - Austkin,http://www.austkin.net/index.php?loc=language&id=1073,"Austkin is a database on Australian Aboriginal kinship and social organization or social category systems such as sections, moieties, subsections etc. It contains hundreds of kinship terminologies from over 500 Australian languages and dialects, and allows for historical, anthropological and linguistic perspectives and studies on kinship and its change.",Wik Ngathan,Australian
3,Wik-Ngathan - Sorosoro,https://www.sorosoro.org/en/wik-ngathan/,"Maps Sutton, Peter. 1978. Wik: Aboriginal society, territory and language at Cape Keerweer, Cape York Peninsula, Australia. University of Queensland: PhD. Sutton, Peter. 1995. Wik-Ngathan dictionary. Adelaide: Caitlin Press. Smith, Ian and Johnson, Steve. 2000. Kugu Nganhcara. In Handbook of Australian languages Vol. 5, eds. Dixon RMW and B ...",Wik Ngathan,Australian
4,Wik-Ngathan - Pama Language Centre,https://www.pamacentre.org.au/wik-ngathan/,"The dialect group consisting of Wik-Ngathan and Wik-Ngatharr/Wik-Alken are endangered by language shift to another Indigenous language, Wik-Mungkan, as well as English. Though the dialects Wik-Ngathan and Wik-Ngatharr/Wik-Alken share similar lexicon and grammar there is significant dialect and intra-dialectal variation.",Wik Ngathan,Australian
5,Wik-Ngathan Linguistic Notes and Sources - Pama Language Centre,https://www.pamacentre.org.au/wik-ngathan-linguistic-notes-and-sources/,"The site-mapping database (Sutton et al. 1990) includes Wik-Ngathan language data. (2) The archive of Ursula McConnel includes an extensive collection of photographic documentation of the Wik area, field notes and recorded and transcribed texts. These materials include a number of Wik-Ngathan-related materials.",Wik Ngathan,Australian
6,A pan-dialectal documentation of Wik-Ngathan and Wik-Ngatharr: Cape ...,https://www.elararchive.org/dk0192,"Wik-Ngathan and Wik-Ngatharr/Wik-Alken are Paman language varieties spoken on the west coast of Cape York Peninsula (CYP), Australia. Speaker numbers have significantly declined as the younger generation shift to the lingua franca of the area, Wik- Mungkan, and English. This documentation project involves working with speakers of Wik- Ngathan and Wik-Ngatharr to collect a range of transcribed ...",Wik Ngathan,Australian
7,Garry Namponan - Wik & Kugu Art & Craft Aboriginal Corporation,https://wikandkuguarts.com/artist/garry-namponan/,"Garry's mother's country is Aayk and her language being Wik-Ngathan.. Garry's father, Angus Namponan was a prominent Wik carver in Aurukun. Most of his sons have followed in his footsteps. Garry's brothers, Lex, Leigh, Bevan and Leo are established and emerging carvers and form an important core of artists within the Wik and Kugu Arts ...",Wik Ngathan,Australian
8,Wik Ngathan language - globalrecordings.net,https://globalrecordings.net/en/language/wig,"Wik Ngathan language and dialect information. Audio Bible stories and lessons. Download free evangelism resources, MP3s, audio bible study tools, language/dialect information.",Wik Ngathan,Australian
9,Wik-Ngathan dictionary / Peter Sutton - National Library of Australia,https://catalogue.nla.gov.au/catalog/2092729,Wik-Ngathan - English dictionary and English finderlist; pronunciation guide; portraits of Wik-Ngathan people.,Wik Ngathan,Australian
